# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Wikipedia clickstream dumps: ~484 MB each, re-downloadable with
# `python tools/clickstream.py fetch`. The derived weights are committed instead.
tools/clickstream-*.tsv.gz

__pycache__/

# Koppen-Geiger source bundle: 130 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB file limit, and 71 of its
# 72 GeoTIFFs are future SSP scenarios or resolutions nothing reads. The single grid
# used is extracted and committed as koppen_geiger_0p1_1991_2020.tif (217 KB).
# Re-fetch: https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/61012822
tools/geo-cache/koppen_geiger_tif.zip

# IBTrACS best-track archive: 143 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB file limit. The derived
# per-country storm counts are committed as geo-cache/cyclone_storm_counts.csv instead.
# Re-fetch: https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/data/international-best-track-archive-for-climate-stewardship-ibtracs/v04r01/access/csv/ibtracs.since1980.list.v04r01.csv
tools/geo-cache/ibtracs.since1980.list.v04r01.csv
# Natural Earth reefs: fetched, evaluated, and not used -- see derive_physical.py.
tools/geo-cache/ne_10m_reefs.geojson
